# Internal AI-assistant guide (kept locally, not published)
AGENTS.md

# ── Bundled agent skills (product content, not local scratch) ──
# Harness directories hold per-machine state and the bare `skills/` rule above
# hides every skills tree, so the skill DocHarvest ships is re-included
# explicitly. Scoped to one directory on purpose: an open `skills/` negation
# would also publish unrelated local skills. Git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded, hence the directory negation first.
!.omp/skills/
# Re-ignore the siblings so only the shipped skill escapes the `skills/` rule.
.omp/skills/*
!.omp/skills/docharvest/
!.omp/skills/docharvest/**
# The packaged skill inside the Python package must ship as well. The bare
# `skills/` rule above matches at ANY depth, so it also hid
# `src/gitbook_downloader/skills/`: the canonical skill was missing from git
# and therefore from every wheel built from a clone, while local tests still
# passed because the files existed on disk. `tests/test_skills.py` guards this.
!src/gitbook_downloader/skills/
# Everything else under it stays ignored (__pycache__, stray notes) so the
# negation cannot sweep build byproducts into the commit.
src/gitbook_downloader/skills/*
!src/gitbook_downloader/skills/__init__.py
!src/gitbook_downloader/skills/docharvest/
!src/gitbook_downloader/skills/docharvest/**
